WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I'm great. How are you?

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm wonderful.
You look fantastic.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.370 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on the first
season of "The Conners."

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:09.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-This show was "Roseanne."

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, it wasn't.
-Yes.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.080 line:92%
-And so, Roseanne, you know,

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.483
she was relieved of her duties,
so to speak.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.617 line:92%
How has it been, you know --

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously,
you still have Laurie Metcalf,

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.620 line:92%
you still have Sara Gilbert.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has it been strange
without Roseanne around?

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was.
It was -- It was really odd.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.460
She's a -- We used to have
a lot of fun on the show,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I really missed her
this year.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I can only imagine
what it's like.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.766
I mean, certainly,
there were things she was doing

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
outside the show which
ultimately led to her leaving,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.937 line:92%
but the product the first year

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
really did have
that old snap to it.

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:43.143
-Well, she -- she gave up a lot
so that we could do the show.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
She gave up
all her rights to it.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we didn't have
to call ourselves the Monners

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the Chonners
or anything like that...

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...and invent new characters.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah,
she will always be missed.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the things that people
loved about the reboot

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the show
is it took issues seriously,

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.994 line:92%
and up to and including the fact

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Roseanne
was written off the show.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her character
died of an opioid overdose.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, and that --

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just kind of say,
"Oh, gosh.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.805 size:78% position:39%
You guys went into it
headlong like that.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you surprised that
that's how they handled it?

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was.
That's pretty permanent.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
when I died on the show,

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
they just brought me back.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You're back, yeah.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're not gonna remember.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:30.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody was watching
toward the end.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He was sleeping.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.094 size:81% position:41%
-And some pretty great
guest stars this year.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Mary Steenburgen.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mary Steenburgen.
Peter Gallagher.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:41.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
Katey Sagal.
The fabulous Estelle Parsons.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic. Yeah.
-She's amazing.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.839
But, yeah.
We got good people on the show.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I know I've forgotten...
half of --

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:51.211
-You'll hear from them.
-I put it in the variety.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.645 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, that's great.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:56.449
We were talking backstage,
your old former castmate,

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.617 line:92%
Jeff Bridges, was on stage,

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
winning an award
at the Golden Globes.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
there were multiple clips

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
of "The Big Lebowski"
in his honor.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:08.428
Is that the film that people
approach you about the most?

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's a good one, man.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.533 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.302
-I did one called "C.H.U.D."
that gets a lot of airplay.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"C.H.U.D."?
-Yeah.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Cannibalistic --

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.707 size:84% position:42%
-Cannibalistic humanoid
underground dwellers.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
"C.H.U.D." was a big deal.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:25.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
I worked in a rental store
and "C.H.U.D." was a big deal.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:25.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.581
Back when people had to go
to a store to get a movie, yeah.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.318 line:92%
But, I mean, people must --

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.187
I would assume that when people
interact with you

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "The Big Lebowski,"
they also --

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
they want to yell
lines of dialogue.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they do.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:41.728 line:92%
What do you hear the most?

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Shut the [bleep] up, Donny."
-Yeah.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
See, that's --

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
I guess that's a weird thing,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.801
because obviously
they're doing that out of love,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
but in doing it,
they're screaming,

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.070 line:92%
"Shut the [bleep] up," to you.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.073
-It's not as bad as when Buscemi
gets it on the street.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's true.
Poor Steve Buscemi.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
I, of course --
It was a Coen Brothers film.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I believe maybe
the first time I saw you

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:04.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
was "Raising Arizona,"
which is --

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.818 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:08.221
But I will say both of those --
-Yeah.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Both of those movies
hold up so well,

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.124 line:92%
because they really weren't

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
specific to the time
they were made.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were they big rentals?
-They were huge rentals, yeah.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They got rewound?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.198 size:84% position:42% line:92%
They got rewound a lot.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Coen Brothers watchers,
they'll rewind.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
They really do rewind well.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got hit with one
of those blue --

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:27.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Lawsuit?
-No, no, not a lawsuit.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:28.942 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:31.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
You robbed some bank.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.845
-And one of those blue pellets.
-Yeah.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.814
-As a special effect,
was that one of the better ones

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:35.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've been involved in?
-It was great.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:39.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, it was great.
I think we only did it twice,

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:42.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of the hours
it involved in cleaning up.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:49.028
It was a teller put a bomb into
the bag of money and fooled us.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which was --
Never mind.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No, but...

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.633
I mean, it was the greatest
thing, because it exploded

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just on you guys
but also on the windshield.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And we were trying to drive.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:01.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Go see the movie, folks.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Out now.
-Rent it.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:03.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Out now.
-And rewind it.

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:06.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Rewind it.
Be kind and rewind.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- What were the movies --
I mean, 'cause again,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:12.118
that was a really inspirational
movie for me growing up.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:12.652 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What were yours?

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:13.987
What were the films that you saw
as a kid that made you --

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.588 size:78% position:39%
-"On The Waterfront."
-"On The Waterfront."

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"On The Waterfront."
I loved it,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it made me
want to try to act.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:24.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And did you ever meet Brando?
-No.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would've --
No. I'm better off.

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Better off, yeah.
You don't think --

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.303 line:92%
Because did he continue to be

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone who was
very important to you?

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:32.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Absolutely. Yeah.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
Especially when
I was starting off.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:37.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you can't
steal everything from him.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.177 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.980
-'Cause you wind up doing
really bad imitations.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Um..."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:47.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did Brando on "SNL," yes?
-Yeah, I did.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"Jeopardy!"

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right.
-"Celebrity Jeopardy!"

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Celebrity Jeopardy!"
Yeah.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.828 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-With Turd Ferguson.

